      "comment": "What one dies of goes in the ablative: <span lang=\"la\">famē morī</span>, to die of hunger (Cic. Att. 6.1.6, Lewis &amp; Short). Plants die too: a bush <span lang=\"la\">sī exāruit, moritur</span>, if it dries out, dies (Varr. LL 5.102). <span lang=\"la\">Moriar, sī …</span>, may I die if … (Cic. Att. 8.6.4)."
